# CHG-2034 (approved): production's Macie examines the directory backups weekly for sensitive data, the organization's
# own types among it (CUI markings, employee numbers), and sends its findings to the security topic; the target runs no
# data discovery, which blocks the move once DFARS 252.204-7012 holds it to FedRAMP Moderate (CHG-2029). The target
# turns on Defender for Cloud's sensitive data discovery (the Defender CSPM extension) over its backups container, with
# the same own data types (Purview custom sensitive information types: set up by hand) and its findings exported to
# the security workspace.
dn: cn=dspm,ou=bindings,env=prod,cloud=target,ou=environments,dc=ciam-ops
changetype: add
objectClass: top
objectClass: ciamDataDiscovery
cn: dspm
ciamBindingRole: data-discovery
ciamScansRole: backup-target
ciamCustomIdentifier: cui-marking: CUI//[A-Z][A-Z/-]*
ciamCustomIdentifier: employee-id: EA[0-9]{6}
ciamRescanDays: 7
ciamFindingsRole: security-findings
ciamProviderRef: /subscriptions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/providers/Microsoft.Security/pricings/CloudPo
 sture/SensitiveDataDiscovery
ciamChangeRef: cn=CHG-2034,ou=changes,dc=ciam-ops
